WEBVTT

00:04.390 --> 00:07.740
So this is Maskviana, 
the biggest kingdom in Yoana.

00:07.740 --> 00:09.480
It's full of people.

00:09.480 --> 00:12.390
That's all you've got to say 
about coming home?

00:12.870 --> 00:15.850
<i>The human realm. My birthplace.</i>

00:16.290 --> 00:19.610
<i>Is this really my...</i>

00:20.250 --> 00:21.890
You there! Miss!

00:22.320 --> 00:24.980
You look like a pilgrim to me.

00:24.980 --> 00:27.430
And if you're going on a pilgrimage, 
how about a robe?

00:27.430 --> 00:28.000
Huh?

00:28.000 --> 00:30.980
This precious garment, 
woven of oliva thread,

00:30.980 --> 00:36.240
was worn by Maskvis the Creator's brother's 
wife's sister's best friend when—

00:35.740 --> 00:36.820
Um...

00:36.240 --> 00:38.910
Then allow <i>me</i> to purchase it.

02:13.980 --> 02:18.990
A Royal Letter and a Taboo Witch

02:19.450 --> 02:23.070
Didn't you hear me? If it's as 
valuable as you say, I insist.

02:23.330 --> 02:25.750
It would make a fine gift 
for His Royal Majesty.

02:25.750 --> 02:27.550
N-No, perish the thought.

02:27.550 --> 02:29.660
Now, if you'll excuse me.

02:30.220 --> 02:31.720
Thank you so much.

02:31.720 --> 02:33.600
Are you on a pilgrimage?

02:33.600 --> 02:34.800
No, I'm—

02:34.800 --> 02:39.570
I am Ocelot, and I have the great honor 
to serve as the acting commander of

02:39.570 --> 02:41.750
the Kingdom of Maskviana's 
Exorcistic Knights.

02:42.020 --> 02:43.160
Ah...

02:43.940 --> 02:48.110
To reach Lova Cathedral, 
go two streets over and head north.

02:48.110 --> 02:49.560
No, I'm—

02:49.560 --> 02:51.810
Atria Abbey, then?

02:51.810 --> 02:56.700
That's in the hills outside of town, 
but it's a bit far to set out now.

02:56.700 --> 02:59.240
This guy ain't gonna listen.

02:59.240 --> 03:02.140
Um, I'm actually looking for the palace.

03:02.140 --> 03:04.650
I want an audience with the king.

03:04.650 --> 03:08.620
An audience? His Majesty doesn't 
grant those to just anyone.

03:08.620 --> 03:11.370
But I'll hear you out if you'll let me.

03:11.370 --> 03:12.770
Thank you!

03:15.000 --> 03:17.330
My name is Sariphi.

03:17.330 --> 03:20.620
I'm an emissary from the king 
of Ozmargo, the beast realm,

03:20.620 --> 03:24.550
and I bear a letter to the king of 
Maskviana, who represents Yoana.

03:27.010 --> 03:28.470
I got arrested.

03:28.470 --> 03:30.120
Well, duh.

03:30.120 --> 03:34.640
Did you expect them to buy that 
you came from the beast realm?

03:34.910 --> 03:41.590
But they'll believe me when they find 
out the letter is real, won't they?

03:41.590 --> 03:43.360
I wouldn't be so sure.

03:43.880 --> 03:45.530
I hope Ocelot

03:46.320 --> 03:50.720
actually reports the letter to his king.

03:51.750 --> 03:55.710
Oh, will Lady Sariphi truly be safe?!

03:55.990 --> 03:58.560
Sh-She'll be fine, Princess Amit.

03:58.560 --> 04:02.510
Sari's a human in a human land! 
She'll be in no danger!

04:02.510 --> 04:03.410
No danger!

04:03.720 --> 04:07.840
I dunno. What if hearing she's 
a beast envoy freaks them out?

04:07.840 --> 04:10.210
She could be locked up right now.

04:12.110 --> 04:14.440
B-Be strong!

04:14.440 --> 04:15.390
Eee!

04:16.930 --> 04:20.150
I mustn't go on like this.

04:20.630 --> 04:26.500
After all, there's someone who must be far 
more beside himself with worry than I am.

04:27.450 --> 04:28.740
Namely, His Majesty.

04:30.720 --> 04:32.690
It's nighttime.

04:33.360 --> 04:36.020
What'll we do if they just leave us here?

04:36.020 --> 04:39.340
What <i>can</i> we do, except 
settle down here for life?

04:39.340 --> 04:41.500
We can't do that!

04:41.500 --> 04:43.200
Sariphi Kleinoel.

04:44.600 --> 04:46.180
Pardon this delay.

04:46.180 --> 04:50.890
I have confirmed that your name is indeed 
that of the most recent sacrifice.

04:51.470 --> 04:55.410
As such, we will provisionally accept that 
you have traveled here from the beast realm.

04:55.410 --> 04:57.600
Then what about the letter?

04:57.890 --> 05:02.440
Unfortunately, beast script is 
currently taboo in this kingdom.

05:02.440 --> 05:04.320
Thus, none here can read it.

05:04.950 --> 05:09.620
And I cannot deliver the paper to His 
Majesty without knowing its contents.

05:09.620 --> 05:10.500
What?

05:10.500 --> 05:11.590
Oh, come on.

05:12.290 --> 05:16.160
However, I hear tell that a 
woman in a frontier village

05:16.160 --> 05:19.160
is engaged in independent 
study of beast script.

05:29.050 --> 05:30.350
She may be able to—

05:30.350 --> 05:31.230
I'll go!

05:31.560 --> 05:33.230
I'd like to pay her a visit!

05:33.230 --> 05:34.450
You would...

05:39.250 --> 05:43.980
Very well. Bring her here 
to decipher the missive.

05:43.980 --> 05:47.810
If it is as you say, I will see 
that His Majesty receives it.

05:50.550 --> 05:53.840
You sure about this, girlie? 
You agreed awful quick.

05:54.260 --> 05:58.610
Yes. He said she studies beast script, 
even though it's forbidden.

05:59.080 --> 06:02.960
If there really is a woman like that, 
I want to meet her!

06:04.080 --> 06:09.850
<i>I wonder what made her interested in 
beast culture, and how she feels about it.</i>

06:10.430 --> 06:11.410
What?!

06:11.410 --> 06:15.520
You don't mean the Witch 
of Shidai, do you, miss?!

06:15.760 --> 06:16.870
What witch?

06:16.870 --> 06:21.240
A girl who lives on her own, 
way out that way.

06:21.240 --> 06:25.970
They call her a witch in these parts 
'cause she reads beast writing, I hear.

06:28.370 --> 06:29.690
That the place?

06:30.510 --> 06:34.690
Um, excuse me! Hello!

06:37.500 --> 06:38.980
Maybe she's out?

06:52.840 --> 06:55.210
Hey! What the hell was that for?!

07:00.170 --> 07:01.090
<i>She looks...</i>

07:05.420 --> 07:06.810
I said,

07:06.810 --> 07:08.500
give it a rest!

07:11.340 --> 07:13.870
<i>I was right. She looks...</i>

07:14.910 --> 07:19.560
<i>like His Majesty's—like Leo's other form.</i>

07:22.130 --> 07:24.510
That's enough, Bennu.

07:28.520 --> 07:29.420
Are you—

07:29.420 --> 07:33.370
Who are you? How did you tame this monster?

07:33.370 --> 07:35.580
Who're you calling a monster?!

07:35.580 --> 07:37.060
Now, now.

07:37.480 --> 07:39.380
I'm Sariphi.

07:39.380 --> 07:41.790
I used to be a sacrifice,

07:41.790 --> 07:45.180
but a lot happened, and now I'm 
an emissary for the beast realm.

07:46.490 --> 07:47.680
You're <i>what</i>?

07:48.060 --> 07:50.520
I came here to ask you for a favor.

07:50.520 --> 07:53.610
I heard that you can read beast script, so I...

07:54.370 --> 08:00.540
I don't know what the villagers told you, 
but it has nothing to do with me.

08:01.410 --> 08:02.370
Leave.

08:02.620 --> 08:04.220
Oh, wait!

08:04.220 --> 08:06.270
I have more questions for—

08:07.670 --> 08:12.330
I want nothing to do with beasts, 
even as a prank.

08:12.760 --> 08:16.580
I have nothing to tell you, 
and I don't want to hear your story.

08:17.840 --> 08:18.900
Begone.

08:19.290 --> 08:21.110
Next time, I really will kill you.

08:24.530 --> 08:27.970
That lady's got an even worse 
temper than I figured.

08:28.460 --> 08:30.870
She's a witch, all right.

08:33.800 --> 08:38.580
<i>A sacrifice? The beasts' emissary? 
What in the world...</i>

08:40.730 --> 08:44.090
<i>But it's got nothing to do with me.</i>

08:48.190 --> 08:50.530
Are you kidding me, girlie?

08:50.530 --> 08:55.270
You're gonna camp out in these 
hills until she'll deal with you?

08:55.270 --> 08:58.130
Yup. I can't leave empty-handed.

08:58.650 --> 09:02.000
The king'd faint if he found out.

09:02.000 --> 09:04.220
Don't tell him, okay?

09:04.220 --> 09:06.360
He can't understand me anyway.

09:06.600 --> 09:10.610
Not that that lady seems 
much for listening, either.

09:11.190 --> 09:15.190
Speaking of which, you said you 
had more questions for her.

09:15.720 --> 09:16.770
Yes.

09:17.500 --> 09:19.930
<i>I can't even tell Bennu</i>

09:20.400 --> 09:24.070
<i>that I'm curious because she looks 
like the king's human form.</i>

09:24.790 --> 09:25.860
<i>And...</i>

09:26.690 --> 09:28.060
Begone.

09:28.060 --> 09:29.530
<i>Those cold eyes.</i>

09:30.590 --> 09:35.480
<i>For a moment, I felt scared, as though 
His Majesty had said that to me.</i>

09:40.100 --> 09:40.300
<b>TA-</b>

09:40.100 --> 09:40.300
<b>DA</b>

09:40.100 --> 09:40.300
<b>TA-</b>

09:40.100 --> 09:40.300
<b>DA</b>

09:40.300 --> 09:40.850
<b>TA-</b>

09:40.300 --> 09:40.850
<b>DA</b>

09:40.300 --> 09:40.850
<b>TA-</b>

09:40.300 --> 09:40.850
<b>DA</b>

09:40.670 --> 09:42.230
Good morning!

09:42.230 --> 09:43.300
Yo.

09:45.840 --> 09:48.260
Wait! Hear me out!

10:05.530 --> 10:08.630
Jeez! Talk about unapproachable.

10:08.630 --> 10:09.700
Yeah.

10:13.590 --> 10:15.170
Where's she going?

10:24.040 --> 10:25.600
Edelweiss.

10:26.720 --> 10:27.920
Right?

10:28.610 --> 10:30.850
Are you growing these flowers?

10:31.450 --> 10:32.990
So what if I am?

10:33.500 --> 10:36.160
What's wrong with a witch growing flowers?

10:36.160 --> 10:37.710
"A witch"? Really.

10:38.170 --> 10:40.140
That's just a nickname.

10:40.140 --> 10:42.450
What are you really called?

10:46.690 --> 10:48.060
I forget.

10:59.150 --> 11:00.120
Rain...

11:02.040 --> 11:03.910
We should head back, too.

11:03.910 --> 11:04.760
Yeah.

11:13.820 --> 11:14.570
Huh?

11:21.420 --> 11:22.670
What are you doing?!

11:24.360 --> 11:26.180
Who're you?!

11:26.180 --> 11:27.580
No, who are <i>you</i>?

11:27.940 --> 11:30.310
This is the witch's garden!

11:30.310 --> 11:36.470
Yeah! She grows poison here to 
kill us villagers from Shidai!

11:37.450 --> 11:38.520
What?

11:38.890 --> 11:41.540
There's nothing poisonous about edelweiss!

11:41.870 --> 11:44.980
No, that can't be!

11:44.980 --> 11:47.530
Her blood is cursed!

11:47.530 --> 11:49.170
She's a dreadful witch!

11:51.830 --> 11:53.530
Wh-What the?!

11:53.530 --> 11:55.780
Stay out of this!

11:55.780 --> 11:58.730
We need to destroy this field of poison quick!

11:58.730 --> 12:01.200
I'll never let you do that!

12:01.200 --> 12:04.520
Could she be one of the witch's minions?!

12:04.830 --> 12:06.000
Tie her up!

12:07.030 --> 12:07.820
Hey!

12:08.550 --> 12:09.760
<i>Sire...</i>

12:12.820 --> 12:13.910
B-Blood!

12:14.330 --> 12:17.500
Yes, this is a witch's garden.

12:18.220 --> 12:22.600
If you set foot in it, come prepared to die.

12:23.380 --> 12:25.030
I-It's her!

12:37.240 --> 12:39.450
Th-Thank you.

12:40.360 --> 12:42.940
I just got rid of a threat to my field.

12:43.870 --> 12:47.660
If you keep hanging around, 
I'll do the same to you.

12:50.840 --> 12:52.620
Why did you go this far?

12:53.100 --> 12:54.290
They're only flowers.

12:55.540 --> 12:56.570
Well...

12:57.410 --> 13:03.300
These flowers, edelweiss, 
stand for precious memories.

13:03.950 --> 13:06.460
So I thought that maybe you grow them

13:06.460 --> 13:12.970
to remind you of something 
you really care about.

13:19.510 --> 13:22.520
Don't let anything the 
villagers say bother you.

13:22.520 --> 13:24.530
You're not a witch.

13:24.530 --> 13:26.750
I'll get strong enough to prove it.

13:29.230 --> 13:32.840
I'll practice the sword like mad 
and learn horse riding, too.

13:32.840 --> 13:36.320
I'll run every day and polish 
myself till I shine.

13:37.270 --> 13:39.410
There's no way you could do all that!

13:40.450 --> 13:44.250
What could a wimp like you ever prove?!

13:44.520 --> 13:45.870
Just leave me alone!

13:46.320 --> 13:47.990
Stop coming to see me!

14:02.780 --> 14:05.400
I never knew these flowers had that meaning.

14:05.880 --> 14:10.350
An old friend of mine from 
the village used to grow them.

14:12.480 --> 14:13.670
That's all.

14:15.490 --> 14:18.450
You said you're called Sariphi, right?

14:19.970 --> 14:22.320
Don't you have a favor to ask me?

14:22.770 --> 14:25.140
I'll hear you out, but no promises.

14:25.540 --> 14:26.590
You mean it?!

14:26.590 --> 14:28.270
Nice going, girlie!

14:28.270 --> 14:30.980
Once you get 'em talking, the rest is easy.

14:31.350 --> 14:33.810
All right, then. Tell me your name.

14:34.080 --> 14:34.980
Huh?

14:34.980 --> 14:36.510
Your name.

14:37.090 --> 14:37.890
Huh?

14:38.970 --> 14:42.560
What? <i>That's</i> your question?

14:42.560 --> 14:43.230
Yup.

14:44.340 --> 14:47.620
I mean, you're not really a witch,

14:48.330 --> 14:51.600
so I want to know what to call you.

14:55.530 --> 14:57.020
Anastasia.

14:58.260 --> 14:59.820
It's Anastasia.

15:01.630 --> 15:03.200
Anastasia...

15:05.760 --> 15:06.900
Hey, are you...

15:08.030 --> 15:08.910
Huh?

15:14.890 --> 15:16.850
You okay, girlie?

15:19.500 --> 15:22.430
Here. Dry yourself off with that.

15:22.430 --> 15:26.370
Th-Thank you for taking care of me.

15:26.950 --> 15:31.230
If you'd died there, your rotting 
carcass would be a nuisance.

15:32.970 --> 15:35.330
You're so nice, Asya.

15:36.100 --> 15:37.870
Hey, Asya.

15:39.050 --> 15:40.500
"Asya"?

15:40.500 --> 15:43.590
You're Anastasia, right? 
So "Asya" for short.

15:46.760 --> 15:48.550
Get some sleep.

15:48.890 --> 15:51.050
Okay.

16:04.840 --> 16:09.250
Did your fever break? You must 
be tougher than you look.

16:10.940 --> 16:12.820
You're up late, Asya.

16:13.410 --> 16:14.910
What are you reading?

16:16.470 --> 16:17.280
This is...

16:18.010 --> 16:19.720
a book in beast script!

16:20.790 --> 16:25.770
I came looking for you because there's 
some beast script I'd like you to read.

16:26.200 --> 16:27.040
What is this?

16:27.750 --> 16:29.490
Just a diary.

16:30.140 --> 16:34.600
One of my female ancestors made 
a point to write it in beast script.

16:35.290 --> 16:38.230
She must not have wanted anyone 
in the village to read it.

16:38.760 --> 16:40.790
But how did she learn beast script?

16:42.770 --> 16:45.140
Oh, if you'd rather not say...

16:45.140 --> 16:46.400
I don't mind.

16:47.480 --> 16:50.160
Generations ago, one of my ancestors

16:50.160 --> 16:54.530
broke a taboo so great that our 
whole lineage is despised for it.

16:55.560 --> 16:57.350
Although she was human,

16:57.990 --> 17:00.630
she made love to a beast and bore his child.

17:01.840 --> 17:05.880
<i>Could that beast have been...</i>

17:06.510 --> 17:08.130
<i>His Majesty's ancestor?</i>

17:08.590 --> 17:10.300
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

17:10.300 --> 17:11.710
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

17:11.710 --> 17:13.100
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

17:13.100 --> 17:14.900
You there, servants.

17:14.900 --> 17:16.240
Explain yourselves.

17:16.580 --> 17:19.800
Did I not warn you against removing so 
many books from the archives at once?

17:20.000 --> 17:23.750
Well, you see, Sari was 
planning to read these.

17:24.130 --> 17:26.930
We're bringing them back to the archives now.

17:26.930 --> 17:27.780
Now.

17:30.150 --> 17:34.360
Where did you get this book? 
Was it in the archives, as well?

17:34.630 --> 17:37.040
Huh? Don't recognize.

17:37.040 --> 17:39.180
That's strange.

17:39.700 --> 17:40.500
Oh!

17:40.900 --> 17:43.070
It must be Justice Set's!

17:43.070 --> 17:46.030
I bet it slipped in when 
he bumped into Sari!

17:48.520 --> 17:50.300
Your ancestor and a beast...

17:50.840 --> 17:54.330
Then... do you have beast blood, too, Asya?

17:54.550 --> 17:55.800
I don't know.

17:56.160 --> 17:59.810
What became of my ancestor who 
married a beast is a mystery, too.

18:00.430 --> 18:06.350
But this diary proves that my 
family was linked to a beast.

18:06.870 --> 18:10.740
I deciphered beast script to read it,

18:11.430 --> 18:14.510
but it's full of boring, everyday stuff.

18:15.780 --> 18:19.230
<i>The diary of someone who loved a beast.</i>

18:19.590 --> 18:21.490
If you want it, you can have it.

18:21.840 --> 18:23.820
I was going to get rid of it anyway.

18:23.820 --> 18:25.130
Are you sure?

18:25.970 --> 18:30.500
Yeah, although I don't know why you're 
so interested in someone's diary.

18:31.070 --> 18:37.480
Something about someone dear 
to me might be written in it.

18:38.260 --> 18:40.690
Sometimes I still ponder, even now.

18:41.550 --> 18:45.520
Did the mother whom I've never seen love me?

18:46.720 --> 18:52.940
Did anyone wish for my birth?

18:54.380 --> 19:02.000
It might give me answers that would mean 
a lot to my beloved—to His Majesty.

19:02.970 --> 19:05.860
Your "beloved"? "His Majesty"?

19:06.880 --> 19:08.830
He's the king of beasts.

19:09.990 --> 19:11.010
You...

19:11.280 --> 19:15.570
I can't imagine falling for a beast.

19:16.000 --> 19:17.800
To be honest, it makes me sick.

19:18.850 --> 19:19.850
But...

19:22.080 --> 19:25.420
Anyway, what do you need me to do?

19:25.690 --> 19:26.440
Huh?

19:26.440 --> 19:27.180
Girlie.

19:27.650 --> 19:32.150
I'd like you to decipher a letter 
written in beast script.

19:32.690 --> 19:35.100
Please come with me to the palace.

19:37.060 --> 19:39.680
<i>Wait for me, sire.</i>

19:44.130 --> 19:45.210
Wait.

19:46.410 --> 19:48.070
Where do you think you're going,

19:48.310 --> 19:49.310
Set?

19:51.110 --> 19:53.520
Why feign ignorance?

19:53.520 --> 19:56.740
This path leads to only one place.

19:57.080 --> 20:03.010
The forbidden archive, which only 
royalty and select priests may enter.

20:03.280 --> 20:09.460
You know that as well as I do. 
Is that not why you shadow me so often?

20:09.460 --> 20:11.750
<i>He noticed.</i>

20:11.750 --> 20:13.440
Oh, that book.

20:13.860 --> 20:17.330
That's the one I lost the other day.

20:17.330 --> 20:18.630
I see.

20:19.160 --> 20:23.940
Only royalty and the archpriest, 
second in power to the king,

20:23.940 --> 20:26.620
may read that forbidden volume.

20:27.430 --> 20:31.340
Though the archpriest vanished 
during His Late Majesty's reign,

20:31.340 --> 20:33.940
and the post has long been vacant.

20:34.680 --> 20:38.630
I have read what only such great men may.

20:39.000 --> 20:45.700
Merely entering this taboo realm requires 
arts known only to royals and priests,

20:45.700 --> 20:48.470
and yet I set foot in there and took that.

20:49.130 --> 20:53.540
And now that you're certain of it, 
you've come to confront me.

20:53.540 --> 20:55.410
Am I correct?

20:55.900 --> 21:00.120
How can you be so calm, scoundrel?

21:00.120 --> 21:03.020
Don't you realize that your trespasses—

21:03.020 --> 21:03.620
Yes.

21:03.980 --> 21:09.490
Breaking this taboo is treason 
and an affront to royal dignity.

21:09.490 --> 21:10.570
Unless...

21:10.880 --> 21:14.540
the perpetrator is royalty himself.

21:15.920 --> 21:19.010
Set, what are you...

21:19.420 --> 21:26.520
My Lord Chancellor, your line has 
endured to serve the royal house.

21:26.950 --> 21:30.300
True, but I chose the king of my own will!

21:30.300 --> 21:33.650
His Majesty is the only one for 
whom I would give everything!

21:34.040 --> 21:37.140
Yes, how truly touching.

21:37.630 --> 21:40.850
But have you ever asked yourself

21:40.850 --> 21:44.320
who your king <i>truly</i> is?

21:45.180 --> 21:46.820
Chancellor,

21:46.820 --> 21:51.740
<i>you</i> should know the truth 
about the absolute monarch

21:52.730 --> 21:54.940
to whom you pledged everything.

23:25.950 --> 23:31.270
I'm so glad Asya opened up to 
me after that frosty reception.

23:31.270 --> 23:35.520
But should I really have accepted this diary?

23:35.520 --> 23:39.480
What if it says something His Majesty 
would want to keep private?

